# pain001 signing keys
#
# Commits and release tags in this repository are signed with SSH keys
# (git's gpg.format=ssh), not OpenPGP, so this file is in OpenSSH
# allowed-signers format rather than an ASCII-armoured keyring.
#
# Verify a commit or tag:
#
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile KEYS.asc
#   git verify-commit HEAD
#   git verify-tag v0.0.66
#
# Every line below is "principal keytype base64-key". A key is added by
# the maintainer in a signed commit; a key is retired by removing its
# line, also in a signed commit, so the history of this file is the
# trust log.
#
# Maintainer: Sebastien Rousseau
sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIDjGRQyeM79nAb4GHcpGzXMKq7HE3xyEOev4gVsnBN1e
